{
  "_about": "events/list, tools/list and the manifest for the sample events, as events-list.json pins them today. The samples are events-list.json's three, each now with an explicit access setting, plus deploy.finished: chat.message has public: true, game.turn personal: true (as today), ci.run declares nothing (tools-only, the default), and deploy.finished has an authorize that allows everyone (arguments {env: string, required, \"The environment\"}, payload {status: string, required, \"How it ended\"}, no text). events/list lists only the events a native client may subscribe to (personal, authorize or public), so ci.run is absent; subscribe_events lists the same; unsubscribe_events names every event, since unsubscribing stays allowed on every path. tools holds only the built-ins (no vendor tools), shape-normalized as in events-list.json (README.md), without outputSchema (tool-output-schemas.json pins those). Order: events and manifest in definition order (chat.message, game.turn, ci.run, deploy.finished); tools by name. Replaces events-list.json when PR 6 and PR 10 land.",
  "_status": "FINAL (compact tools/list bench, 2026-11-05: compact matched or beat the baseline in every cell). compact_strings in subscribing-tools-list.json is the one place these strings live; every literal that uses them (wake-args.json compact, subscribes.json compact_cases, event-tools.json, events-list.json tools, subscribing-tools-list.json scenarios, tool-output-schemas.json) is generated from it.",
  "_c1_dependent": {
    "manifest[*].subscribe": "C1: the manifest's per-event subscribe, \"tools\" or \"any\" (personal, authorize and public send \"any\"). public itself isn't sent: the core only needs \"any\"."
  },
