  "_vouchers": "Subscribe vouchers (docs/subscribe-vouchers.md §4.3): while the core's manifest answer reports features [\"subscribe_vouchers\"], events/list to a native request (ChatGPT, or a client that declares the MCP Events extension) also lists tools-only events, in definition order with the others, each as the vendor wrote it, with delivery [\"webhook\"] only (events/poll of a tools-only event is refused, voucher or not), plus a required wakeshift_voucher string described with the app's name (event-tools.json voucher_argument; app is what GET /app names, \"this app\" when it names none). events_native is the whole list for a native request with the feature on (here ci.run, the tools-only sample); a bridged request, or any request without the feature, gets events above unchanged. The manifest is unchanged.",
